title: Carving Fork
text: A SPLITTER is a half-silvered mirror: half the light goes straight through it and half bounces off at a right angle, so one beam becomes two. Hit it face-on and the bounced half goes straight back. Give the fork its second tine.
trick: one beam split in two
motif: two-tined carving fork
expect: shared>=1
---
L 7 14 0 g
*S 7 10 1 k
*R 10 10 1 k
% handle
T 7 12 0 ?
% the bar between the tines
T 8 10 0 ?
% tines
T 7 3 0 ?
T 10 3 0 ?
